# ── personal data: never commit ──
# (git does NOT support inline comments — every comment must be its own line)
#
# Allowlist, not denylist. Everything the pipeline generates under corpus/ is
# derived from real chats and carries real names, and each new stage used to need
# its own rule here — one missing line is how 13 months of history and a 732-entry
# address book once got staged for a public repo. Ignore the directory and name
# the exceptions instead, so a stage added later is private by default.
corpus/*
!corpus/README.md

# ── local config: tokens, phone numbers, group IDs ──
config/*.json
config/*.json5
config/*.tsv
config/*.txt
!config/examples/
!config/examples/**

!docs/screenshots/

# ── guard state ──
guard/tripped.json

# ── secrets ──
.env
*.key
*.pem
credentials/

# ── python / node ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
